From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: sppc: authentication data, licensing events; kernelbase: FlsGetValue2, TlsGetValue2, QueueUserAPC2, WerRegisterCustomMetadata

Word's licensing thread calls SLSetAuthenticationData at start; it was a
stub, and Word ended with 0xe0000002 before its window came up. The rest of
what programs call is filled in: authentication data is accepted and there
is never a result to read (SL_E_VALUE_NOT_FOUND); licensing events register
and never fire; genuine information reads as not found and is accepted;
the machine is genuine locally (SLIsGenuineLocalEx); re-arm and setting the
current key succeed; offline activation is not offered.

Word and Office's AI component also ask kernel32 for newer functions:
FlsGetValue2 and TlsGetValue2 (the slot, leaving the last error alone),
QueueUserAPC2 (a special APC is queued as an ordinary one; Wine has no
special APCs), WerRegisterCustomMetadata / WerUnregisterCustomMetadata
(error reports are never sent: accepted).

Gate: test/sppc-gate.sh (make test-sppc).

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/thread.c
@@ -376,6 +376,25 @@
 
 
 /***********************************************************************
+ *           QueueUserAPC2   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * Stained Glass OS: newer Windows' form, with flags. A special user APC runs
+ * without the thread waiting alertably; Wine has none, so it is queued as an
+ * ordinary one -- it runs at the thread's next alertable wait. (Office's
+ * threads look for it and fall back to nothing when it is missing.)
+ */
+BOOL WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH QueueUserAPC2( PAPCFUNC func, HANDLE thread, ULONG_PTR data, DWORD flags )
+{
+    if (flags & ~1u /* QUEUE_USER_APC_FLAGS_SPECIAL_USER_APC */)
+    {
+        SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    return QueueUserAPC( func, thread, data ) != 0;
+}
+
